      "worked_solution": "Since $\\triangle ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overline{AB}$, we have that $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{AC}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =AC \\\\ 4x-3 & =2x+1 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this value into the expression for the measure of $\\overline{AB}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =x+4 \\\\  & =(2)+4 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AB=6.$",
